# Typography & Fonts (Design System)

## Font stack (Tailwind + index.html)

| Role | Tailwind class | Font | Use for |
|------|----------------|------|---------|
| Body / UI | `font-sans` (default) | DM Sans | All body text, labels, buttons, inputs |
| Headings | `font-display` | Space Grotesk | Page titles, section titles, card titles |
| Accent | `font-serif` | Instrument Serif | Optional: quotes, editorial accents |
| Code / keys | `font-mono` | System monospace | Doc keys, kbd, technical IDs |

## Rules

1. **Use semantic headings** — Prefer `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>` so base styles in `src/index.css` apply (they set `font-display` and size scale). Do not override with `font-sans` on headings unless intentionally de-emphasizing.

2. **Non-semantic titles** — If you use a `<div>` or `<span>` for a hero/section title, add `font-display` so it matches headings: e.g. `className="font-display text-2xl font-bold"`.

3. **Do not** introduce new font families or load extra Google Fonts without updating both `index.html` and `tailwind.config.ts` and this rule.

4. **Mono** — Use `font-mono` for document keys, API IDs, keyboard shortcuts (e.g. `<kbd className="font-mono">`).

5. **Weights** — Use `font-medium`, `font-semibold`, `font-bold` as needed; avoid inline `font-weight` values so the design scale stays consistent.
